# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers for privileged surfaces (Issue #654)
#
# GitHub requires a listed code owner's approval on any pull request that
# touches a path matched below, once the "Require review from Code Owners"
# branch-protection rule is enabled on the default branch (Develop). This
# closes the poisoned-pipeline / secret-exfiltration path where a workflow
# edit runs with privileged secrets the moment CI fires — before a human
# necessarily notices the workflow diff. The workflows here reference
# secrets beyond the default GITHUB_TOKEN: the write-capable ACTIONS_PUSH
# PAT (deno-security-update.yml, deno-outdated.yml), SEMGREP_APP_TOKEN
# (semgrep.yml) and CODECOV_TOKEN (quality.yml).
#
# Owner teams MUST have write (push) access to this repository, otherwise
# GitHub silently ignores the rule. @stSoftwareAU/developers is the
# maintaining team with push access, matching the sibling NEAT-AI repo.

# CI/CD surface — all GitHub Actions workflows.
/.github/workflows/  @stSoftwareAU/developers

# The CODEOWNERS file itself, so ownership rules cannot be quietly changed.
/.github/CODEOWNERS  @stSoftwareAU/developers

# Supply-chain scripts — same blast radius as the workflows that run them.
/bump-deps.sh  @stSoftwareAU/developers
/bump_deps.ts  @stSoftwareAU/developers
/quality.sh    @stSoftwareAU/developers
